menu "Knob moon display"

config KNOB_MOON_TEST_EPOCH
    int "UTC epoch for the static frame (until knob_time lands, K7d)"
    default 1794175200
    help
        The K7b static moon renders this UTC instant (default
        2026-11-08T22:00Z -- the milestone's bench date, so the disk
        can be compared against the published phase of the day).
        K7d's knob_time (esp_sntp over the existing Wi-Fi join)
        replaces this with the real instant; until then the moon view
        never claims a "now" it does not have. This value is USED
        again only under KNOB_TIME_USE_TEST_EPOCH (bench builds):
        production arms exclusively on an SNTP fix, never here.

config KNOB_DEMO_MODE
    bool "Knob demo mode: scripted phase tour (bench comparison)"
    default n
    help
        The knob side of the on-device demo tour (docs/
        verification/demo-mode, mirrors the clocks' UI_DEMO_MODE).
        After the boot presentation (the static frame) the producer
        task walks EIGHT canonical phases of the current synodic month
        (new moon -> waning crescent, epochs pinned at k/8 of the
        month) plus a ninth step on the LIVE current phase (re-baked
        every cycle, events on), holding each for
        KNOB_DEMO_PHASE_SEC. The power ladder stays held (no dim, no
        deep sleep) so a recording never goes dark; the caption shows
        the phase name. Every step logs `phase=<name> cycle=<n>`
        (tag DEMO) for the recording harness. Production builds keep
        this off.

config KNOB_DEMO_PHASE_SEC
    int "Knob demo mode: seconds per phase step"
    depends on KNOB_DEMO_MODE
    default 15
    range 5 600

endmenu
